## Project Overview
       VoteLite is a web-based voting system that lets registered voters cast their ballots online and 
lets an administrator watch the results update in real time. The administrator manages the 
candidates (names, offices, and photos), voters identify themselves with a Voter ID, choose 
their candidates, review the ballot, and submit it. Every submitted ballot is reflected immediately 
on the admin dashboard without refreshing the page.

## Features

**Voter page**
- Enter Voter ID and Full Name 
- Pick candidates per office; each candidate shows a photo (or initials) beside the name
- Only offices that have candidates appear on the ballot
- Review the ballot, then submit and see a "Vote Recorded" screen
- One ballot per Voter ID

**Admin page ("Sentro ng Halalan")**
- Live stats, chart, and results per office
- Add candidates with a name, office, and optional photo
- Change photo, edit, or remove candidates

## Tech Stack

Node.js, Express, Socket.io, Chart.js, HTML/CSS/JavaScript. Data is stored in memory,
so it resets when the server restarts.

1.1 Objectives
•Provide a simple, clear, and trustworthy ballot interface for voters.
•Give the administrator one place to manage candidates and monitor results live.
•Enforce basic election rules: one ballot per Voter ID and a maximum number of choices per office.
•Show results instantly using real-time communication (WebSockets).

## How to Run

1. Install Node.js
2. `cd backend`
3. `npm install`
4. `npm start`
5. Open the address shown in the terminal (usually http://localhost:5000), then go to `/voter.html` or `/admin.html`

Internet is needed for Chart.js and Google Fonts.

