*Important note*

This project was developed as a learning activity to apply the concepts and lessons
we learned in Event-Driven Programming (EDP). It demonstrates how event-driven 
programming works through a voting system, particularly how different events,
user interactions, and functions work together to perform specific actions.

Please note that this is only a demonstration project and is not yet a fully
reliable or production-ready voting system. Some features, such as permanent database 
storage, admin authentication, verification against an official registered-voter list,
and stronger security measures, have not yet been implemented.

However, these limitations can be addressed through further development. 
We believe that the system can still be improved and expanded by implementing 
additional features, integrating a proper database, and strengthening
its security and reliability.

The main goal of this project is to apply our knowledge of
Event-Driven Programming in a practical way, demonstrate
what we have learned, and gain experience in designing
and developing a functional system.

















